This document describes how the openssl program was packaged for build2. In
particular, this understanding will be useful when upgrading to a new upstream
version. See ../README-DEV for general notes on OpenSSL packaging.

Symlink the required upstream files and directories into openssl/:

$ ln -s ../../upstream/{apps,include/internal} openssl

Symlink the libcrypto private header that apps/lib/cmp_mock_srv.c includes
as "../../crypto/cmp/cmp_local.h", so that this path also resolves in the
distribution, where the apps/ symlink is replaced with its target:

$ mkdir -p openssl/crypto/cmp
$ ln -s ../../../../upstream/crypto/cmp/cmp_local.h openssl/crypto/cmp/

Copy upstream's auto-generated apps/progs.{h,c} into openssl/. Note that these
files are not platform-specific.
